#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.10"
# dependencies = [
#   "numpy>=1.24.0,<2.0",
#   "pandas>=2.0.0,<3.0",
#   "pyarrow>=14.0.0",
#   "duckdb>=0.10.0",
#   "pyyaml>=6.0",
#   "scipy>=1.10",
# ]
# ///
"""ant-ucell — UCell scoring from the genesetstore into scores.parquet.

UCell (Andreatta & Carmona 2021, Comput Struct Biotechnol J) is a rank-based
enrichment scorer. For each cell, all genes are ranked by expression
(descending, rank 1 = most expressed). The score for a gene set S of size k
in a gene universe of size n is the normalized Mann-Whitney U statistic:

    U        = sum(rank(g) for g in S) - k*(k+1)/2
    score    = 1 - U / (k * (n - k))

This equals the AUROC of the set-gene ranks vs background-gene ranks:
score = 1 means every set gene outranks every background gene; score ≈ 0.5
is random. No top-N threshold is applied — the full rank distribution is
used, which makes UCell more robust than AUCell on sparse single-cell data
where the threshold choice strongly affects the recovery curve.

Differences from ant-aucell:
  - Algorithm: Mann-Whitney U on full ranks (UCell) vs AUC with top-5% threshold (AUCell).
  - Dependencies: pure numpy/scipy — no pyscenic/ctxcore required.
  - Source string in scores.parquet: 'ucell' (not 'aucell').
  - Input: the dataset's duckdb layer (by-cell parquet sidecar), not the h5ad.
  - min_n gate, Ensembl autodetect, status semantics: identical to ant-aucell.

Cell type scope (2026-10-08): a module is scored only on the cells whose cell
type belongs to the module's ``celltypes`` group (``lib/celltype_scope.py``:
``group_of`` of the dataset's ``ant_cell_type`` per cell against
``lib/celltype_groups.yaml``); ``celltypes: [all]`` and ``role: markers``
modules are scored on every cell. Cells outside the scope get no row (NULL).
UCell ranks the genes within each cell, so a cell's score does not depend on
which other cells are scored (no control-gene sampling as in scanpy). The
cells of a scope are therefore read from the duckdb and ranked in chunks of
``--chunk-cells`` (default 50000): peak memory follows the chunk (sparse
expression plus one rank batch), not the dataset, and the scores are the same
for any chunk size. Each catalog is written once, atomically, after all chunks. An
experiment with no matching cell in the dataset is not scored and its stale
``ucell`` sidecar rows are removed.

Scores are written to the dataset's ``<basename>.scores.parquet`` sidecar with
source='ucell' so they coexist with aucell, geneset, and starcat scores.

The sidecar is immediately queryable via:
  GET /databases/<db>/module_score?source=ucell&catalog=<experiment>

Reference:
  Andreatta M & Carmona SJ (2021). UCell: Robust and scalable single-cell
  gene signature scoring. Comput Struct Biotechnol J 19:3796-3798.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.csbj.2021.06.043

Usage:
  ant ucell <db_id> <experiment_or_geneset_id> [<id>...]

Examples:
  ant ucell M23/AST Habib2020/DAA_states_human
  ant ucell Z20/MIC Sierksma2025/WGCNA
  ant ucell Z20/MIC Sierksma2025/WGCNA Mancuso2024/Cell_states
  ant ucell Z20/MIC Sierksma2025/WGCNA --overwrite
  ant ucell Z20/MIC Sierksma2025/WGCNA --dry-run
  ant ucell Z20/MIC Sierksma2025/WGCNA --min-n 3

Options:
  --min-n N          minimum gene overlap required to score a module (default 5)
  --overwrite        re-score even if (source='ucell', catalog=<experiment>)
                     already exists in scores.parquet
  --layer NAME       expression layer (default: .md default_layer, else X)
  --chunk-cells N    cells loaded and ranked at a time (default 50000)
  --dry-run          score but do not write
  -v, --verbose      per-module stats
"""

